///THIS IS AN UPDATE TO NRC REPORT NUMBER 1468288. THE UPDATE IS THAT THE RELEASE ORIGINATED FROM THE PIPELINE UNDERGROUND, THE AMOUNT OF RELEASE IS 3800 BARRELS AND THE MATERIAL IS CONTAINED.///

///ORIGINAL///
THE CALLER STATES THAT AN UNKNOWN LOCAL FIRE DEPARTMENT DISCOVERED A  RELEASE OF DIESEL, INTO THE YARD, FROM AN ABOVE GROUND VALVE ON AND  UNDERGROUND 36" TRANSMISSION PIPELINE AT THE BOOSTER STATION. THE CALLER STATES THE CAUSE OF THE RELEASE WAS DUE TO EQUIPMENT FAILURE.

/// POTENTIAL RELEASE ///


CALLER STATES THEY RECEIVED A REPORT OF A SUNKEN VESSEL IN SHALLOW WATER IN THE MORADA BAY ANCHORAGE AREA.

02 ENGINES ON BOARD; TYPE/AMOUNT OF POTENTIAL RELEASE IS UNKNOWN.

NO SHEEN REPORTED AT THIS TIME


/// POTENTIAL RELEASE ///

/// THIS IS A POTENTIAL RELEASE ///


CALLER REPORTS AN ACTIVE VESSEL FIRE ON A 28' WHITE AND BLUE PACEMAKER, AGROUND IN THE OTTAWA RIVER.  THERE IS A POTENTIAL RELEASE OF AN UNKNOWN AMOUNT OF UNKNOWN FUEL ON BOARD. IT IS ESTIMATED TO HAVE A FUEL CAPACITY LESS THAN 100 GALLONS.


/// THIS IS A POTENTIAL RELEASE ///

///THIS IS A 48 HR PHMSA UPDATE TO NRC REPORT 1468182///

UPDATE: SERVICE LINE IS NOT DOT-REGULATED. THE INCIDENT WAS CORRECTED TO INDICATE THAT A FIRE WAS INVOLVED AND IT HAS BEEN EXTINGUISHED. DAMAGES HAVE OCCURRED BUT THE TOTAL COST IS UNKNOWN.

ORIGINAL: CALLER IS REPORTING A LARGE FIRE AT AN APARTMENT COMPLEX WITH A POTENTIAL RELEASE OF NATURAL GAS.  CALLER STATED THERE ARE 14 RISER AT THE  BUILDING.  CLASS 8 AND CLASS 2 FEED TO THE BUILDING.

/// POTENTIAL RELEASE ///   

THE CALLER REPORTED A TUG WAS TOWING A 656FT NON TANK CARGO CARRIER VESSEL IN THE CORPUS CHRIST CHANNEL AT THE INCIDENT LOCATION. THE CALLER STATED WHILE THE TUG WAS SWINGING THE NON TANK CARGO CARRIER AROUND TO DOCK THEM THE TUG MADE CONTACT WITH THE NON TANK CARGO CARRIER FOR UNKNOWN REASONS. THE CALLER STATED THERE IS AN UNKNOWN AMOUNT OF OIL / FUEL / MATERIALS ON BOARD THAT COULD POSSIBLY RELEASE. 

-NO INJURIES OR FATALITIES.

/// THIS IS A CORRECTION TO NRC REPORT 1468040 ///

THE CALLER ORIGINALLY REPORTED THIS AS A POTENTIAL RELEASE. THIS REPORT CORRECTS THIS TO AN ACTUAL RELEASE.

/// ORIGINAL REPORT BELOW ///

THE CALLER REPORTED THE DISCOVERY OF AN UNKNOWN SHEEN FROM AN UNKNOWN  SOURCE ON THE WATERS OF THE INTERCOASTAL WATERWAY.

/// THIS IS A 48 HR PHMSA UPDATE TO NRC REPORT # 1467965 ///


UPDATE:
CALLER STATES THAT ALTHOUGH THE CAUSE IS UNKNOWN, AN EXPLOSION WAS INVOLVED; INCIDENT IS STILL UNDER INVESTIGATION 

ORIGINAL:
CALLER REPORTED THAT A 1-INCH STEEL SERVICE LINE WAS STRUCK BY A SKID STEER AND IGNITED, RESULTING IN A STRUCTURE FIRE. AN UNKNOWN AMOUNT OF NATURAL GAS RELEASED. THERE IS ONE REPORTED INJURY. THE TOTAL COST IN DAMAGES IS CURRENTLY UNKNOWN.


/// THIS IS A 48 HR PHMSA UPDATE TO NRC REPORT # 1467965 ///

/// THIS IS A CORRECTION TO NRC REPORT # 1468162 ///

CORRECTION:
CORRECT INCIDENT CAUSE IS EXPLOSION, NOT OPERATOR ERROR.


