UPDATE:
CALLER STATES THAT ALTHOUGH THE CAUSE IS UNKNOWN, AN EXPLOSION WAS INVOLVED; INCIDENT IS STILL UNDER INVESTIGATION 
ORIGINAL:
CALLER REPORTED THAT A 1-INCH STEEL SERVICE LINE WAS STRUCK BY A SKID STEER AND IGNITED, RESULTING IN A STRUCTURE FIRE. AN UNKNOWN AMOUNT OF NATURAL GAS RELEASED. THERE IS ONE REPORTED INJURY. THE TOTAL COST IN DAMAGES IS CURRENTLY UNKNOWN.
/// THIS IS A 48 HR PHMSA UPDATE TO NRC REPORT # 1467965 ///


/// THIS IS A CORRECTION TO NRC REPORT # 1468162 ///

///THIS IS AN UPDATE TO NRC REPORT NUMBER 1467875. THE UPDATE IS THAT THERE HAS BEEN ONE CONFIRMED FATALTITY AT THIS TIME.///

///ORIGINAL///
CIC REPORT 

****THIS IS A POTENTIAL RELEASE REPORT****
REPORT OF A CHARTER VESSEL CAPSIZING IN SAN FRANCISCO BAY WITH (15) PEOPLE  ON BOARD. (8) OUT (15) HAVE BEEN RESCUED.

///THIS IS A 48 HR PHMSA UPDATE TO NRC REPORT 1467862///

UPDATE: THE VOLUME OF MATERIAL RELEASED HAS BEEN UPDATED TO 308 GALLONS FROM 226 GALLONS. THE SPILL ORIGINATED FROM FACILITY PIPING AT A TANK FARM, NOT FROM A STORAGE TANK, AND THE REPORT HAS BEEN UPDATED TO REFLECT THAT INFORMATION. THE REPORTING PARTY CONTACT EMAIL ADDRESS HAS BEEN CORRECTED.

ORIGINAL: THE CALLER DISCOVERED STANDING DIESEL FUEL IN THE OIL MANIFOLD, AS A RESULT OF LEAKING PIPING.

///THIS IS A 48 HR PHMSA UPDATE TO NRC REPORT 1467884///

UPDATE: THE QUANTITY RELEASED HAS BEEN UPDATED FROM 3.5 MMCF TO 3.6 MMCF. THE CALLER CONFIRMED THAT NO IMPACTS TO TRANSPORTATION OCCURRED (ROAD/RAILROAD/WATERWAY CLOSURES) AND THERE WERE NO DAMAGES OR ENVIRONMENTAL IMPACT.

ORIGINAL: THE CALLER REPORTED A RELEASE OF APPROXIMATELY 3.5 MMCF OF NATURAL GAS FROM A COMPRESSOR STATION THAT WENT INTO THE AIR AT THE INCIDENT LOCATION. THE CAUSE OF THE RELEASE IS DUE TO A SUCTION VALVE FAILING TO CLOSE.

/// THIS IS AN UPDATE TO NRC REPORT 1467685 ///

THE CALLER STATED THAT WHILE CONNECTING THE FLOW LINE TO THE JUMPER A HANDHELD TORQUE TOOL RELEASED THE MATERIAL IN QUESTION. THE CAUSE OF THE TOOL RELEASING THE MATERIAL IS UNKNOWN AND CURRENTLY THE CALLER IS WORKING TO RETRIEVE IT. ONCE RETRIEVED AN INVESTIGATION WILL BE CONDUCTED INTO THE CAUSE. 

/// ORIGINAL REPORT BELOW /// 

	CALLER IS REPORTING A JUMPER FLOW LINE CONNECTOR RELEASED 1.5 OUNCES OF  HYDRAULIC OIL INTO THE GULF DUE TO A FAULTY CONNECTION. RELEASE SECURED AND NO CLEAN UP EFFORTS REPORTED. CALLER HAD NO FURTHER INFORMATION.

/// THIS IS AN UPDATE TO NRC REPORT 1467745 /// 

THE UPDATE IS AS FOLLOWS: AFTER FURTHER INVESTIGATION INTO THE LOCATION A CHANGE HAS BEEN MADE TO REFLECT A MORE ACCURATE LOCATION. 

/// ORIGINAL REPORT BELOW /// 

THE CALLER STATES THE SRP HAS DUMPING MATERIALS (SALVAGE POOL) AND A  COMBINATION OF OIL AND OTHER MATERIALS ARE POOLING ON THE SOIL.

/// POTENTIAL RELEASE ///   

THE CALLER REPORTED A CATAMARAN VESSEL CAPSIZED IN THE PACIFIC OCEAN AND WASHED ASHORE IN APRA HARBOR DUE TO HEAVY WAVES AT THE INCIDENT LOCATION. THE CALLER STATED THERE IS APPROXIMATELY 30 GALLONS OF GASOLINE, AND 2 GALLONS OF LUBE OIL ON BOARD THAT CAN POTENTIALLY DISCHARGE. 

-FIVE PEOPLE WERE RESCUED OFF OF THE VESSEL. NO INJURIES OR FATALITIES.

/// THIS IS A CORRECTION TO NRC REPORT 1467656 /// 

THE CORRECTION IS AS FOLLOWS: THE ORIGINAL REPORT IS NOT LISTED AS A POTENTIAL RELEASE. THIS REPORT CORRECTS THIS ISSUE. 

/// ORIGINAL REPORT BELOW /// 

THE CALLER STATED THAT A VESSEL CAPSIZED DUE THE VESSEL GOING TOO FAST ON A WAKE. CURRENTLY THERE HAS BEEN NO RELEASE OF MATERIAL, HOWEVER THE POTENTIAL FOR AN UNKNOWN AMOUNT OF UNKNOWN OIL TO BE RELEASED IS PRESENT. THE MATERIAL HAS THE POTENTIAL TO IMPACT THE KAHULUI HARBOR.

/// THIS IS AN UPDATE TO NRC REPORT 1467638 ///

THE UPDATE IS AS FOLLOWS: THE CALLER STATED THAT (2730) POUNDS OF NOX RELEASED OVER A 24-HOUR PERIOD FOR THE 12TH OF JULY. 

/// ORIGINAL REPORT /// 


	THE CALLER STATED THAT THE PLANT AT THE LOCATION WENT DOWN. BECAUSE OF THIS NOX RELEASED IN UNKNOWN AMOUNTS. ALTHOUGH THE AMOUNT OF MATERIAL THAT  RELEASED IS UNKNOWN THE CALLER SUSPECTS IN EXCESS OF (1000) POUNDS MAY HAVE RELEASED. THE CAUSE OF THE RELEASE WAS A LOSS OF PROPANE COMPRESSORS AT THE LOCATION.

/// THIS IS AN UPDATE TO REPORT 1467655 ///

UPDATE AS FOLLOWS: THE AMOUNT OF NATURAL GAS RELEASED WAS DETERMINED TO BE 992 MCF.

ORIGINAL REPORT AS FOLLOWS: 	THE CALLER STATES A TREE FELL DURING THUNDERSTORMS, AND BROKE OFF A 1-INCH  VALVE, CAUSING A RELEASE OF NATURAL GAS. 2 HOMES WERE EVACUATED AS A  PRECAUTION. 

THE CALLER EXPECTS GREATER THAN (3000 MCF) WHICH IS THE RQ.

/// THIS IS AN UPDATE TO REPORT 1467655 ///

/// THIS IS AN UPDATE TO REPORT 1467603 ///

UPDATE AS FOLLOWS: SMALL AMOUNTS OF SHEEN ARE STILL VISIBLE GOING INTO THE RIVER, PRIMARILY SILVERY. THE DISCHARGE POINT IS ABOUT A 10 BY 10 FOOT AREA. STILL ATTEMPTING TO CONTAIN THE RELEASE. CONTAINMENT AND ABSORBENT BOOM HAVE BEEN DEPLOYED.

ORIGINAL REPORT AS FOLLOWS: 	THE CALLER REPORTED A DISCOVERY OF AN UNKNOWN SHEEN FROM AN UNKNOWN SOURCE  IN AN OUTFALL AT A CHEMICAL MANUFACTURING FACILITY THAT ENTERED INTO THE  NECHES RIVER AT THE INCIDENT LOCATION. THE CALLER STATED THEY HAVE  CONDUCTED VISUAL SURVEYS OF THE FACILITY, AND HAVE NOT BEEN ABLE TO FIND  ANY EVIDENCE THAT THE UNKNOWN SHEEN WAS FROM THE FACILITY. THE CALLER  STATED THERE ARE NEIGHBORING ROADS THAT MAY BE THE SOURCE OF THE SHEEN, BUT AT THIS TIME THE SOURCE OF THE SHEEN IS UNKNOWN.

/// THIS IS AN UPDATE TO REPORT 1467603 ///

/// POTENTIAL RELEASE ///   

THE CALLER REPORTED A 72FT FISHING VESSEL IS TAKING ON WATER IN LAKE UNION DUE TO A HOLE IN THE VESSEL AT THE INCIDENT LOCATION. THE CALLER STATED THERE IS APPROXIMATELY 1000 GALLONS OF DIESEL FUEL, 50 GALLONS OF HYDRAULIC OIL, AND 40 GALLONS OF MOTOR OIL ON BOARD THAT CAN POTENTIALLY DISCHARGE.

-THERE ARE 3 PERSONS ON BOARD (NOT IN DANGER) THAT THEY ARE ATTEMPTING TO GET OFF OF THE VESSEL.

/// THIS IS AN UPDATE TO NRC REPORT 1467550 ///

THE CALLER CHANGED THE MATERIAL RELEASED FROM SULFURIC ACID TO HYDROCHLORIC ACID.

/// ORIGINAL REPORT BELOW ///

THE CALLER REPORTED A FIRE AT A MANUFACTURING FACILITY. THE CAUSE OF THE  FIRE IS UNKNOWN. THIS RESULTED IN THE RELEASE OF ABOUT 5000 GALLONS OF  SULFURIC ACID (LESS THAN 12%) INTO A CONTAINMENT AREA. ABOUT 1000 GALLONS  ESCAPED CONTAINMENT ONTO NEARBY SOIL. NO WATERWAYS OR STORM DRAINS WERE  AFFECTED. THE FIRE HAS BEEN EXTINGUISHED.

THE RELEASE CAME FROM ACID TANKS 1, 2, AND 3, EACH OF WHICH ARE FIXED AND  HAVE A 12,000 GALLON CAPACITY.

///THIS IS AN UPDATE TO NRC REPORT 1467452///

UPDATE: THE RQ WAS ONLY EXCEEDED ON SULFUR DIOXIDE, 595 POUNDS RELEASED.

ORIGINAL: CALLER IS REPORTING A POWER OUTAGE AT A REFINERY CAUSED THE RELEASE OF AN UNKNOWN AMOUNT OF SO2 AND H2S INTO THE ATMOSPHERE. RELEASE SECURED. INVESTIGATION ONGOING. CALLER HAD NO FURTHER INFORMATION.

/// POTENTIAL RELEASE ///   

THE CALLER REPORTED A MISSING 5 GALLON DRUM OF HAZARDOUS WASTE (CONTAINING PCB'S). THE CALLER STATED A FLAT BED SEMI TRUCK LEFT BISHOP, CA AND TRAVELED APPROXIMATELY 277 MILES TO LOS ANGELES, CA AND DISCOVERED AT THE LOS ANGELES TSDF (TRANSPORTATION STORAGE AND DISPOSAL FACILITY) THAT THE DRUM WAS MISSING. THE WHEREABOUTS OF THE DRUM ARE CURRENTLY UNKNOWN.

-THE DRUM CONTAINS APPROXIMATELY 4.5 POUNDS OF MATERIAL.

///NEEC INCIDENT NOTIFICATION///


2026/07/08 00:39 MCTS SARNIA ADVISED THAT MANITOULIN / XJBX TOUCHED THE 175 HIGHWAY BRIDGE WHILE SECURING AT RIVER ROUGE MORTON SALT. THE VESSEL KNOCKED OUT THE REAR MAST. NO APPARENT DAMAGE TO THE BRIDGE. NO POLLUTION AND THE VESSEL WAS ABLE TO SECURE SAFELY AT DOCK. THE SHIP INTENDS TO SECURE THE MAST, WAIT FOR DAYLIGHT HOURS TO ACCESS
DAMAGE AND FURTHER COURSE OF ACTION.

