///POTENTIAL RELEASE///

CALLER REPORTED THAT A 55 GALLON BLUE DRUM WAS FOUND IN THE ST LAWRENCE RIVER. IT IS UNKNOWN WHAT IS IN THE DRUM AND IT HAS NO LABELS. THERE ARE NO SIGNS OF A RELEASE OR SHEEN, BUT THERE IS A POTENTIAL FOR UNKNOWN MATERIALS TO HAVE RELEASED FROM THE DRUM.

///THIS IS AN UPDATE TO NRC REPORT 1466893///

UPDATED: LESS THAN 1 GALLON OF SODIUM HYDROXIDE RELEASED FROM RAIL CAR UTLX631193 INTO A PLASTIC CONTAINMENT CATCH BASIN USED TO PREVENT MATERIAL FROM RELEASING TO SOIL/GROUND. 

ORIGINAL: 25 RAILCARS DERAILED ON THEIR SIDE.

/// THIS IS A POTENTIAL RELEASE ///


CALLER STATES THEY RECEIVED A REPORT OF A STRUCTURE FIRE AT A HOME, SERVICED BY THEIR NATURAL GAS COMPANY AND SENT A DISPATCH TO THE INCIDENT LOCATION TO INVESTIGATE.

ALTHOUGH UNCONFIRMED, THEY BELIEVE THERE IS A POTENTIAL FOR A LEAK OF AN UNKNOWN AMOUNT OF NATURAL GAS AND THAT AN EXPLOSION MAY HAVE OCCURRED.


/// THIS IS A POTENTIAL RELEASE ///

/// POTENTIAL RELEASE ///   

THE CALLER REPORTED A 17FT CATAMARAN VESSEL CAPSIZED IN THE PACIFIC OCEAN WITH APPROXIMATELY 3-4 GALLONS OF GASOLINE, AND 1 LITHIUM BATTERY ON BOARD THAT CAN POTENTIALLY RELEASE AT THE INCIDENT LOCATION. THE CALLER STATED THE CAUSE OF THE VESSEL CAPSIZING IS UNKNOWN. 

-TWO PEOPLE WERE AIRLIFTED FROM THE WATER NEAR THE VESSEL. NO INJURIES OR FATALITIES.

///CORRECTION TO INCIDENT REPORT # 1466758///

CORRECTION IS AS FOLLOWS: THE COUNTY WILL BE CHANGED FROM HARRISON TO HARRIS. 

ORIGINAL DESCRIPTION IS AS FOLLOWS: THE CALLER IS REPORTING A RELEASE OF LOW PH WATER "LEACHATE WATER", INTO  THE HOUSTON SHIP CHANNEL, FROM A PHOSPHOGYPSUM STACK. THE CALLER STATES  THAT THE CAUSE OF THE RELEASE WAS DUE TO A POND LINER FAILURE.

/// NEEC INCIDENT NOTIFICATION: SHIPWRECK WITH POTENTIAL POLLUTION | ST. MARY'S RIVER | ST. JOSEPH ISLAND, ON ///

CONSTABLE CALLED TO ADVISE THAT THERE IS A BOAT THAT WASHED UP ON SHORE ON SAINT JOSEPH ISLAND IN ONTARIO. THE CURRENT WHEREABOUTS OF THE BOAT ARE UNKNOWN AND THE RCMP ARE CURRENTLY USING DRONES TO TRY TO LOCATE IT. THEY AREN'T ABLE TO FIGURE OUT IF ITS A NEW OR OLD WRECKAGE. 

-THE UNITED STATES COAST GUARD TRACKED DOWN THE OWNER, WHO GAVE THE INTENTION OF PICKING UP THE BOAT TODAY

///THIS IS A 48 HR PHMSA UPDATE TO NRC REPORT 1466793///

UPDATE: THE COORDINATES HAVE BEEN UPDATED TO 39.809769 N 75.428406 W. THE PIPELINE HAS BEEN UPDATED FROM 3" TO 1". THE CALLER REPORTED THAT THIS WAS A VAPOR RELEASE TO AIR AND NOT A LIQUID RELEASE. THE FIRE HAS NOW BEEN EXTINGUISHED AND THE RELEASE HAS BEEN SECURED. USCG AND PA DEP WERE ALSO ON SCENE.

ORIGINAL: THE CALLER DISCOVERED A RELEASE OF PROPANE THAT CAUGHT FIRE FROM A 3" TRANSMISSION PIPELINE. THE CALLER STATES THAT THE PROPANE WAS NOT A VAPOR RELEASE DUE TO THE FIRE. CALLER ALSO STATES THAT THE FIRE HAS NOT BEEN EXTINGUISHED.

/// THIS IS A 48 HR PHMSA UPDATE TO REPORT 1466752 ///

UPDATE AS FOLLOWS: NO SIGNIFICANT UPDATES TO REPORT.

ORIGINAL REPORT AS FOLLOWS: CALLER REPORTED THAT A COOLANT LEAK ON 6/14 CAUSED A COMPRESSOR FIRE WHICH  RESULTED IN THE RELEASE OF 5.3MCF OF NATURAL GAS. THE COST THRESHOLD WAS  CONFIRMED TO BE MET AT 0915 ON 7/2 (ESTIMATED $350,000).

/// THIS IS A 48 HR PHMSA UPDATE TO REPORT 1466752 ///

/// THIS IS A UPDATE TO NRC REPORT 1466679 ///

THE UPDATE IS AS FOLLOWS: THE CALLER STATED THAT THEY ORIGINALLY REPORTED (89) BARRELS RELEASED, HOWEVER IT WAS ACTUALLY (89) GALLONS.

/// ORIGINAL REPORT BELOW /// 

	THE CALLER DISCOVERED A FAILURE ON A WELL, CAUSING 89 BARRELS OF CRUDE OIL  TO RELEASE TO A PAD.

///THIS IS AN UPDATE TO NRC REPORT 1466640///

UPDATE: 256 POUNDS OF MATERIAL RELEASED FROM THE SRV WHICH LIFTED DUE TO OVERPRESSURIZATION. 4 PEOPLE WERE TRANSPORTED, 2 RECEIVED OXYGEN AND 2 NOTHING WAS DONE. 60 EMPLOYEES SHELTERED IN PLACE, AND NO EVACUATION TOOK PLACE. ESTIMATED RELEASE DURATION WAS 16 MINUTES. THE WEATHER WAS CLEAR.

ORIGINAL: AMMONIA RELEASED FROM AN UNKNOWN SOURCE DUE TO AN UNKNOWN CAUSE AT THIS TIME.  CALLER RECEIVED NOTIFICATION OF THE INCIDENT FROM A TEAM MEMBER ONSITE.

///THIS IS A 48 HR PHMSA UPDATE TO NRC REPORT 1466678///

UPDATE: THE SPILL WAS ISOLATED, AND CLEAN UP IS UNDERWAY AND ONGOING. THE RELEASE AMOUNT HAS BEEN UPDATED TO 24.8 BARRELS. THEY PURGED AND BLINDED THE LINE FOR CUTOUT, REFILL OPERATIONS WILL POTENTIALLY OCCUR STARTING TOMORROW.

ORIGINAL: CALLER REPORTING THE RELEASE OF 25 BARRELS OF CRUDE OIL ONTO THE SOIL FROM A PIPELINE DUE TO SUSPECTED CORROSION.

///POTENTIAL RELEASE REPORT///

THE CALLER IS REPORTING A POTENTIAL RELEASE OF AN UNKNOWN FUEL AND MOTOR OIL, INTO HUMBOLDT BAY, FROM A PLEASURE CRAFT THAT CAUGHT ON FIRE. THE CALLER STATES THE CAUSE OF THE ONBOARD FIRE IS UNKNOWN AT THIS TIME.

